# Copy to `.env.local` (not committed). Values are baked in at **`npm run build`** time.

# --- Production / EdgeOne ---
# Pure static HTML **has no** `/api/visits`. You must either:
#
# A) Same host: configure EdgeOne origin/rule so **`GET /api/visits`** (and **`GET /api/visits?inc=1`**)
#    forwards to a Node process running `server/visit-api.mjs` (or equivalent implementing `visit-handler.mjs`).
#
# B) Separate API host: set this before build — the browser will call:
#    `GET ${VITE_VISIT_API_URL}/api/visits?inc=1`
#    Handler already sends `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` for cross-origin GET.
#
# VITE_VISIT_API_URL=https://your-stats.example.com

# --- Local dev ---
# Leave unset: `vitepress dev` serves `/api/visits` via middleware → `server/data/home-visits.json`.
# Optional: `npm run visit-server` if you need the standalone HTTP server on port 3948.
